<% @title = "Meet the Amber crew — Amber Framework" %>
<% @meta = "Meet Amber, Grant, and Gemma through the software responsibilities they represent in the Amber ecosystem." %>

<header class="page-hero character-page-hero">
  <div class="site-container page-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The framework has a crew</p>
      <h1>Big responsibilities.<br>Memorable owners.</h1>
      <p>Amber’s characters make architectural boundaries easier to remember. The personality is playful; the responsibility is real.</p>
    </div>
    <%= image_tag("characters/amber-id-original-studio.webp", class: "page-hero-character", width: "800", height: "800", alt: "Amber, the framework lead") %>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="crew-roster">
        <a class="personnel-card personnel-amber reveal" href="/characters/amber" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><%= image_tag("characters/amber-id-original-studio.webp", width: "800", height: "800", alt: "Portrait of Amber") %></div>
          <div class="personnel-file">
            <span class="file-label">AF-001 · Framework lead</span>
            <h2>Amber</h2>
            <p>Owns the web application’s shape: routing, controllers, ECR views, typed configuration, interaction, and local asset delivery.</p>
            <span class="file-link">Open personnel file · Read docs →</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="personnel-card personnel-grant reveal" href="/characters/grant" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><%= image_tag("characters/grant-id-original-studio.webp", width: "800", height: "800", alt: "Portrait of Grant") %></div>
          <div class="personnel-file">
            <span class="file-label">AF-014 · Records and persistence</span>
            <h2>Grant</h2>
            <p>Runs the data warehouse: models, relations, migrations, transactions, queries, and record keeping.</p>
            <span class="file-link">Open personnel file · Read docs →</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="personnel-card personnel-gemma reveal" href="/characters/gemma" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><%= image_tag("characters/gemma-id-original-studio.webp", width: "800", height: "800", alt: "Portrait of Gemma") %></div>
          <div class="personnel-file">
            <span class="file-label">AF-027 · Files and fulfillment</span>
            <h2>Gemma</h2>
            <p>Handles attachments from intake to delivery: validation, storage, streaming, and organization.</p>
            <span class="file-link">Open personnel file · Read docs →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tinted">
    <div class="site-container open-role-panel reveal">
      <div class="open-role-mark" aria-hidden="true">?</div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsibility map</p>
        <h2>Background work is next.</h2>
        <p>Jobs, retries, schedules, and queues form a separate application boundary. Amber documents that responsibility directly today; a future crew member will represent it only when the name and visual identity are ready.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/amber-way#clear-responsibilities">See how the crew is designed</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
